('nizami street + panaromic city tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','30',30,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nizami Street in Baku is an absolute must-visit! The vibrant atmosphere, beautifully lit streets, and a mix of modern and historic architecture create an unforgettable experience. It’s perfect for a leisurely stroll, shopping at high-end boutiques, or enjoying a meal at one of the many cafes and restaurants. The street truly comes alive in the evening, with its lively vibe and gorgeous lighting. Whether you’re a tourist or a local, Nizami Street offers something for everyone. + Panoramic City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:    -Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital,   opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents  and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and   just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway   (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the   endless stone stairs.)    -Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m.   Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',30.0),
