('boulevard tour + panaromic city tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','30',30,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Walking tour starts along the Baku Boulevard followed by: -Mini Venice of Baku  -Carpet Museum -Deniz Mall   -Ferries Wheel ride   -Carpet Museums  -Boat cruise   -Cristal Hall  -Biking Area + Panoramic City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:    -Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital,   opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents  and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and   just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway   (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the   endless stone stairs.)    -Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m.   Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',30.0),
